# Claude Code: the CLI, and the one tool its status line shells out to.
#
# A cask, because that is how Anthropic ships it -- `cask` and `brew` say where
# Homebrew gets a thing, never what it is for. What matters is that both halves
# live here: the package on this line and the statusLine wiring in apply.sh.
# With the cask in dev-cli instead, enabling this module alone linked a status
# line for a CLI that was never installed.
#
# jq is listed here AND in modules/dev-cli/Brewfile, deliberately. Modules run
# alphabetically and cannot depend on each other, and claude-code sorts before
# dev-cli -- so borrowing dev-cli's copy meant apply.sh had to warn and skip on
# a fresh machine. `brew bundle` is idempotent; a repeated line is cheaper than
# an ordering rule the driver has no way to express.

cask "claude-code@latest" # the CLI itself
brew "jq"          # home/.claude/statusline.sh parses its stdin with it
